  "text": "Sol climbs his ladder, removes the cracked tile and sets it aside.\n\nChoose a shorter part to discuss. Your full writing is still here.\n\nAt Sol’s workbench · Arrange witnessed moments in your own telling\n\nA mixture of flour and liquid that is worked and baked into bread.\n\nTook part in a game or activity, or made music with an instrument.\n\nA flower in Grandma’s garden is waiting to keep its owner’s story.\n\nSol shared A Small Repair with a prepared ending from his account.\n\nThe boy holds his sister’s torn bird. Speak to him before helping.\n\nWould you tell everyone how the repair helped Rina bake the bread?\n\nThe story artwork could not load. Your story and choices are kept.\n\nM3 5c4-2 7-1 9 1 2-2 5-3 9-1v14c-4-2-7-1-9 1-2-2-5-3-9-1V5Zm9 1v14\n\nAn older garden story about two passengers making music together.\n\nPip will carry this message to Grandma. She has not heard it yet.\n\nFood made from dough and baked; a loaf is a whole piece of bread.\n\nA movement of one foot, or a surface used when moving up or down.\n\nSol says: “That's what I'd like to say. I'll add it to the page.”\n\nContinue to have something or make sure it remains a certain way.\n\nAsk Sol whether he wants to finish his ending or bring his draft.\n\nPip read The Torn Wing to Sol and Grandma while Mara was at work.\n\nThe loose end slips! Pip steps back while the bridge comes apart.\n\nA female person already mentioned, or something belonging to her.\n\nM4 9h4l5-4v14l-5-4H4V9Zm12-2a7 7 0 0 1 0 10m3-13a11 11 0 0 1 0 16\n\nContinuing up to this time; when describing movement, not moving.\n\nSol brings his actual manuscript from the workshop to the garden.\n\nThat female person, acting on her own or being referred to again.\n\nPip is carrying her copy. Cross the river and give it to Grandma.",
